{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.KeystonePerronFrobeniusGroundState","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.KeystonePerronFrobeniusGroundState","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Matrix.Mul","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Order.Field.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":9,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.pfGroundState_unit","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.pfGroundState_unit","kind":"instance","line":110,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KeystonePerronFrobeniusGroundState.lean#L110-L122","doc":"**Non-vacuity — the `Unit`-block model over any ordered field.**  One fusion block (`ι = Unit`),\n`N = 1` (the `1×1` identity), `rho = 1`, `d = 1`.  Every positive `v` on `Unit` is `(v ()) • d`, so\n`pf_proportional` holds.  Witnesses that `PerronFrobeniusGroundState` is inhabitable over any ordered\nfield, so `eq_d_of_normalized` / `ground_state_unique` are not conditional-on-`False`.  The OPEN\ncontent is the *physical* instance where `N` is the actual Hecke fusion operator and `d` the Hecke\n`d_q`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.PerronFrobeniusGroundState.ground_state_unique","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.PerronFrobeniusGroundState.ground_state_unique","kind":"theorem","line":97,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KeystonePerronFrobeniusGroundState.lean#L97-L104","doc":"Corollary: two normalised positive ground eigenvectors are **equal** (uniqueness of the pinned\nvalue-map target). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.PerronFrobeniusGroundState.eq_d_of_normalized","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.PerronFrobeniusGroundState.eq_d_of_normalized","kind":"theorem","line":79,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KeystonePerronFrobeniusGroundState.lean#L79-L95","doc":"**The pin (derived, sorry-free): a normalised positive ground eigenvector equals `d_q`.**\n\nGiven the PF class, any positive eigenvector `v` at the Frobenius eigenvalue that is *normalised* to\nagree with `d` at a single index `k` is **equal** to `d` — not merely proportional.  This closes\ninput (B): the value-map target (the `+1` self-dual PF ground state of\n`KeystoneSelfDualSpectralNarrowing`) is uniquely `d_q`.  The proof is genuine (exhibit `c`, evaluate\nat `k`, cancel the nonzero `d k`), so this is a §3b-cond conditional theorem, not a self-assuming\nprojection of `pf_proportional`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.PerronFrobeniusGroundState.pf_proportional","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.PerronFrobeniusGroundState.pf_proportional","kind":"theorem","line":71,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KeystonePerronFrobeniusGroundState.lean#L71-L71","doc":"**Cited PF / Ocneanu–Wenzl uniqueness** (the conjectural input): every positive eigenvector at\nthe Frobenius eigenvalue is a scalar multiple of `d`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.PerronFrobeniusGroundState.d_eigen","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.PerronFrobeniusGroundState.d_eigen","kind":"theorem","line":68,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KeystonePerronFrobeniusGroundState.lean#L68-L68","doc":"`d` is the Frobenius eigenvector: `N d = rho · d`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.PerronFrobeniusGroundState.d_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.PerronFrobeniusGroundState.d_pos","kind":"theorem","line":66,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KeystonePerronFrobeniusGroundState.lean#L66-L66","doc":"The quantum dimensions are positive. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.PerronFrobeniusGroundState.N_nonneg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.PerronFrobeniusGroundState.N_nonneg","kind":"theorem","line":64,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KeystonePerronFrobeniusGroundState.lean#L64-L64","doc":"`N` is entrywise non-negative (the Markov / fusion structure). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.PerronFrobeniusGroundState.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.PerronFrobeniusGroundState.mk","kind":"ctor","line":60,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KeystonePerronFrobeniusGroundState.lean#L60-L60","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.PerronFrobeniusGroundState","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.PerronFrobeniusGroundState","kind":"class","line":51,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KeystonePerronFrobeniusGroundState.lean#L51-L72","doc":"**Perron–Frobenius / Ocneanu–Wenzl ground-state selection** (§3b-cond primary conjecture, `Prop`).\n\nA `Prop`-valued hypothesis class over the **explicit** data `N` (fusion operator), `rho` (Frobenius\neigenvalue), `d` (quantum-dimension vector) — the repo's conditional-class convention\n(`HeckeBraid (H : …) : Prop`), keeping the data explicit and the conjectural assumption\nproof-irrelevant.  Content: `N` non-negative, `d` positive, `d` the Frobenius eigenvector, and — the\nconjectural field — that **any** positive eigenvector at `rho` is a scalar multiple of `d` (PF\nup-to-scale uniqueness).  Primary conjecture (binds no other conjecture class); the content is the\nparameter-quantified `pf_proportional`, not a `True`/empty marker. ","signatureChunk":0}]}